              "question": "<p>Which of the following patients meets the criteria for a comprehensive obesity evaluation as described in this session?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>A 25-year-old with BMI 22 and a family history of type 2 diabetes</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>While a family history of diabetes warrants monitoring, a BMI of 22 does not meet the evaluation threshold. A full evaluation is triggered at BMI ≥23, an obesity-related complication, or weight gain ≥5 kg in 3 months.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>A 35-year-old with BMI 21 who gained 3 kg over 6 months</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Neither the BMI (21, below threshold) nor the weight gain (3 kg in 6 months, below the ≥5 kg in 3 months trigger) meets evaluation criteria.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>A 30-year-old with BMI 24 and no comorbidities</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. By Indian criteria, BMI ≥23 triggers a full evaluation regardless of comorbidities. A BMI of 24 is already overweight and warrants comprehensive assessment.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>A 40-year-old with BMI 22 and mild lower back pain</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A BMI of 22 is below the evaluation threshold of 23, and non-specific back pain is not an obesity-related complication. This patient does not meet the evaluation triggers described.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
