          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>According to the Five As framework for obesity counselling, what is the recommended first step before discussing a patient's weight?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Assess the patient's readiness to change</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Assessment is the second step in the Five As. The framework deliberately places Ask first — seeking permission before initiating a weight discussion — to establish respect and prevent stigma.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Advise dietary modifications</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Advising comes third in the Five As. Jumping straight to advice before seeking permission risks making the patient feel judged. The first step is Ask.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ask permission before discussing weight</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The Five As begin with Ask — seeking permission before discussing weight. This simple step prevents weight stigma, builds trust, and increases the chance of sustained patient engagement.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Agree on realistic weight-loss targets</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Agreeing on goals is the fourth step. The Five As framework deliberately places Ask first — requesting the patient's permission before raising the topic of weight.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The Five As begin with Ask — seeking the patient's permission before discussing weight. Skipping this step risks weight stigma, which drives delayed care and disengagement."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly right. Starting with permission is deliberate — weight stigma drives patients away from care. The Five As (Ask, Assess, Advise, Agree, Assist) provide a non-judgemental counselling structure."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
